Void Mart, episode 10: "Hot Dog Roller" (2026). Original characters, story, pictures and music.

Pictures: drawn in code (canvas 2D) with the Void Mart toon kit (channel/brand/toon.js, channel/brand/vmkit.js, channel/brand/travel.js). The hot dog roller and its fossil hot dogs, the tongs, the bun, the wall clock, MAGS's flavor board and the one-eyed customer are drawn in film.js; the slow time (tau) is computed there and in tools/mix.py from the same curve.
Fonts: Bungee (The Bungee Project Authors) and Fredoka (The Fredoka Project Authors), SIL Open Font License 1.1.
Voices: ElevenLabs text-to-speech, model eleven_v4.
  Pip: "Win2" (owner's own designed voice). Rae: "Kar2" (owner's own designed voice, pitched 1.5 semitones down).
  MAGS: "VM MAGS" (ElevenLabs Voice Design, made for this show). The customer: "Laura" (ElevenLabs default voice).
Sound effects: generated with ElevenLabs Sound Effects (prompts in sfx/prompts.json; five new, five reused from earlier episodes as noted there). The roller's small gear motor and the fluorescent buzz are synthesized in tools/mix.py.
Music: original score for the house jazz trio (tools/band.py, tools/score.py) played with CC0 samples from VSCO 2 Community Edition, VCSL and FreePats.
